    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/7/77803.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 19,
    "turn_text": "It has a lot of economic focus recommendations. So I'm cautiously optimistic that our democratic colleagues will join us. We've tried our best to make these bipartisan, yet tough. And so the select committee is going to be tackling this issue of selective economic decoupling and de-risking. It comes down really huge. We just, at a basic level, as a matter of principle, we don't want to be funding our own destruction. And that's what we've been doing for far too long. And I'm worried that this This revival of engagement, this zombie detente, zombie engagement, is really, it's really satisfies the literal definition of insanity, hoping for a different outcome, despite having tried this over and over again.",
