    "turn_idx": 47,
    "turn_text": "It's corporatizing a movement and it's putting politics at the center of a brand to make money. And people are saying it's enough. There was a time when it was done and brands like Levi's and Target put forth Pride collections that featured rainbow flags on adult t-shirts. And now it's gone so far as to partnering with an artist that features very violent imagery, guillotines and violent copy in their own art. And consumers are saying we've had enough. And if brands are going to say, we are putting politics at the front and center of our advertising campaigns because we think that will make you like us and consumers are well within their rights to say, I reject that. I reject those politics and it doesn't make me like you and I'm not going to",
